hello to you gideon you brought the  complaint that led  to the equality and human rights  commission report are you satisfied with  its findings  very much so this is a report which ends  the debate  it makes very clear that the jewish  community was right  all along we are completely vindicated  whenever everybody said that this was  exaggerated that this was a smear  campaign as jeremy corbyn is still doing  they were wrong and not only were they  wrong they were essentially saying that  jews are liars they were saying that  when we allege anti-semitism we do it  for some kind of political means as part  of some kind of agenda  and that's anti-semitic too and it's not  it didn't take very long after jeremy  corbyn  made his statement this morning for him  to be suspended we  sent our complaint in and minutes later  within the hour we had confirmation that  jeremy corbyn had been suspended  the whip removed and that he was now  subject to  a disciplinary investigation and  this really takes us full circle because  the reason that we referred the labour  party to the equality and human rights  commission in the first place  is that we were making complaints  against jeremy corbyn which for  political reasons due to interference  within the party  were not being investigated and all that  british jews have asked  all along is that british justice be  allowed to  serve its course and today the equality  and human rights commission  issued its report and that as far as  we're concerned  is the beginning of the dispensing of  british justice  jeremy corbyn meanwhile though says he  will contest  the decision to suspend him and remove  the whip and describes it as political  intervention i wonder what you make of  that  the this is what jeremy corbyn has been  saying all along he's been saying it  since 2015 when we first started to  raise concerns about jeremy corbyn back  then  we were vilified there were very few  people who  really understood that anti-semitism  exists on the left as well as the right  and over the years under jeremy corbyn's  leadership  according to our research with yukov and  king's college london anti-semitism on  the far left actually overtook  anti-semitism on the far right so jeremy  corbyn has been making these arguments  for years and the difference now  is that he is a back bencher  a crank who is well  lost uh in the debate he who  has fully lost the debate he is somebody  who  will not see what is real he will not  see that he  presided over a political party which  led to  47 of british jews questioning whether  they had a future in this country and if  you just let that sink in that's the  labour party that created  the equality and human rights commission  then becoming the party  that caused nearly half of an entire  minority community  to question whether they still had a  future in this country  kirsten said today that it was a day of  shame  but that the party will now repair the  grief how does it go about doing that  well the equality and human rights  commission has really spelled out  a very comprehensive set of  recommendations that the labour party  must now  adhere to the labour party has been  given until december  to come up with an action plan that  action plan will have to be agreed with  the equality and human rights commission  and it will actually be enforceable in  court  so this is a uh the road  uh the labour party must travel we have  also made a complaint today  against jeremy corbyn and various other  sitting mps  who were immune from disciplinary  proceedings whilst jeremy corbyn  was leader of the party secure has been  given six months by us  to ensure that those disciplinary  complaints are heard  under the new independent disciplinary  proceedings that the equality and human  rights commission has mandated so  secure has an awful lot of reform to do  but as we see today with the suspension  of jeremy corbyn it's really  he's proving that he can take the labour  party and turn the corner  he has a big fight on his hands as we've  seen people like john mcdonnell  and various other mps who are still  serving labour mps  coming out in force to defend jeremy  corbyn  and really give to amplify his lie  that the jewish community exaggerated  and overstated things for political  purposes those people need to be dealt  with as well  and zakir is going to have a fight on  his hands but we are his ally in that  fight  everybody in the jewish community is  willing him to succeed  and hoping for the day to return when  jews feel safe  within the labour party
 

